      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T18:10:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any java modules that do not specify partition specific properties (e.g. `vendor`, `product_specific`, etc) are considered to be part of the system container by default. This produces a lot of noise in detecting the cts -\u003e system inter-container dependency violations, especially given that `PRODUCT_PACKAGES` reside in make and Soong does not know which modules actually get installed.\n\n`UnstableContainer` is introduced to mitigate this, to detect more common and serious cts -\u003e system dependency violations and reduce noise. Specifically, `UnstableContainer` is marked for modules that are static reverse dependencies of `framework-minus-apex`. Thus, theoretically the `UnstableContainer` is a subset of `SystemContainer`. I believe that this can go away once the partition is migrated to Soong.",
      "parentUuid": "f0ab6565_12bdc043",
